      "body": "## Overview\n\n`VllmConfig.compute_hash()` omits `mamba_config`, so two configs that differ only in Mamba settings collapse to one AOT/compile cache key and reuse each other's compiled artifact. This folds `MambaConfig` into the cache identity.\n\n## Claims\n\n- Bug fix: configs differing only in `mamba_config` now produce distinct compile cache hashes instead of colliding.\n- Covers the Mamba settings that change the compiled mixer: `backend`, `enable_stochastic_rounding`, `stochastic_rounding_philox_rounds`, `ssu_algorithm`.\n- No change to model behavior; only the cache identity is corrected.\n\n## Validation\n\nReproduce the collision on a fresh `VllmConfig`:\n\n```bash\npython -c \"\nfrom vllm.config.mamba import MambaConfig, MambaBackendEnum\nfrom vllm.config import VllmConfig\nc1, c2, c3 = VllmConfig(), VllmConfig(mamba_config=MambaConfig(backend=MambaBackendEnum.FLASHINFER)), VllmConfig(mamba_config=MambaConfig(stochastic_rounding_philox_rounds=4))\nprint(c1.compute_hash(), c2.compute_hash(), c3.compute_hash())\n\"\n```\n\n- Before this change all three print `14d03884cc` (collision). After, they print `30d3023943` / `6bd3c3b2d3` / `b89ca637ad`.\n- `test_vllm_config_hash_covers_mamba` fails without the `mamba_config` factor include and passes with it (red-green).\n- Targeted config hash + mamba tests: `8 passed`. `pre-commit run --files vllm/config/mamba.py vllm/config/vllm.py tests/test_config.py` passes (mypy, SPDX, config-docstring checks).\n- Full `tests/test_config.py` on this head: `43 failed / 454 passed / 9 skipped`. The 43 are pre-existing environmental failures (HF model-download `OSError` for `meta-llama`/`RedHatAI` ids and `test_ir_op_priority_ctx`), none of which touch `compute_hash` or Mamba; the hash/mamba tests all pass. No GPU serving or model-quality evaluation is claimed.\n\nPrepared with AI assistance. I reviewed every changed line and ran the validation above; the pre-existing full-suite environmental failures are kept separate from the change's own evidence.\n\n## Details\n\n`compute_hash` is the identity for the persistent AOT/compile cache (`aot_compile_hash_factors` and the runtime compile cache both key on `vllm_config.compute_hash()`). It is documented to capture every config that affects the graph from input ids to final hidden states. `mamba_config` was missing from the factor list even though it changes the compiled graph:\n\n- `MambaMixer2`'s decode path branches on `mamba_config.backend` and calls a different custom op per backend (`selective_state_update_replayssm_flashinfer` vs `selective_state_update_replayssm_output_only`).\n- `enable_stochastic_rounding` / `stochastic_rounding_philox_rounds` specialize the compiled Triton kernel (e.g. the `USE_RS_ROUNDING` template arg), and `ssu_algorithm` selects the update algorithm.\n\nBecause the traced code hash is identical across these settings (same source files), the config hash was the only separator and it ignored `mamba_config`, so the cache served the wrong compiled artifact. The fix adds `MambaConfig.compute_hash()` (reusing the existing `hash_factors(get_hash_factors(...))` pattern) and folds it into `VllmConfig.compute_hash()` alongside the other always-present configs.\n\nThis is a cache-identity correction: changing Mamba settings now correctly causes a recompile rather than reusing an artifact built for a different backend/kernel.\n\n---\n\n<details>\n<summary> Pull Request Checklist </summary>\n\n- [x] I used vLLM's `/pr-checklist` skill. (Mandatory for agents, optional for humans).\n- [x] AI assistance was used during the creation of this PR.\n\n- [x] **Design Fit:** Minimizes impact on core components, reuses existing functionality, and justifies added complexity.\n- [x] **Testing and Validation:** Validates the change and ensures any added tests are meaningful and reliable, with CI coverage or documented CI resource constraints and validation performed outside CI.\n- [x] **Code Quality and Style:** Keeps code and comments clear and concise, and updates relevant documentation and examples.\n- [x] **Pull Request Contents:** Includes a brief summary and relevant links, supports claims with evidence, explains root causes and implementation trade-offs, and follows the contributing guide.\n</details>\n",
